    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2010370877398151594",
      "url": "https://x.com/Pinas4321/status/2010370877398151594",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/Pinas4321/status/2010370877398151594",
      "text": "STOP STEALING THE SUBWAY: BILLIONS DIVERTED, COMMUTERS BETRAYED\n\nEvery day Filipinos rot in traffic while the administration loot the very project meant to save us from it. The so-called “Project of the Century” is not delayed by engineering—it is being sabotaged by corruption. 🛑\n\nThe Metro Manila Subway, which should have been completed by 2028, is now crawling toward delay because Official Development Assistance (ODA) funds are being deliberately siphoned off to flood control and other high-kickback projects.\n\nFollow the money:\n📍 2024: ₱252 BILLION in ODA funds diverted\n📍 2025: ₱157 BILLION more diverted\n\nThis was supposed to be the BBM administration’s flagship legacy—a finished subway by 2028 that would ease the daily suffering of millions. Instead, it has become another feeding trough for the corrupt. \n\nTHE PRICE OF CORRUPTION:\n\nThe project costs ₱488 BILLION. Because of these delays, the Filipino people will be forced to pay an EXTRA ₱100 BILLION—money stolen from hospitals, classrooms, and social services. \n\nWe are paying for a subway we cannot ride, while the funds meant to complete it vanish into flood control ghost projects and dubious contracts. \n\nThis is betrayal.\n\nCommuters deserve justice.\nThe Filipino people demand accountability. 🇵🇭\n\n#Philippines \n#MetroManilaSubway\n\n✍️Mike Defensor FB",
      "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
